      "groq_label": "New AI models like GPT-6 Astra cost twice as much and run slower for only marginal code review improvements over previous iterations.",
      "groq_discussion": "Discussion type: – Short:\n\nThis article addresses evaluating new AI models like GPT-6 Astra for automated code reviews. Hacker News commenters generally appreciated slight model improvements and believed the project could potentially improve context understanding in code analysis. However, they also expressed concerns about slower processing speeds and higher costs, and questioned the overall utility and noise generated by automated code review tools. Overall, the discussion was largely skeptical, with commenters recognizing both the project's potential and its limitations.",
